        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269">

                <pb facs="0518" n="470" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg470"/>

                <head>No. 269.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Atkinson to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 24, 1877</date>.
                        (Received May 14.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 162.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 161, of
                    yesterday, I now have the honor to inclose to you two printed copies of the text
                    of the proclamation of war on the part of Russia against Turkey, and a
                    translation of the same.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HOFFMAN ATKINSON.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d269-a1.xml" xpointer="d269-a1"/>
            </div>
